<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Zululand (British colony)</h1><p class="st-meta">1887 CE – 1897 CE · capital Eshowe</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British colony created from the remnant of the Zulu kingdom in 1887, incorporated into Natal ten years later.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> and the civil war that followed, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boers</a> had taken the western part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zululand</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nieuwe-republiek">Nieuwe Republiek</a>. To prevent further losses, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> annexed the rest of Zululand in May 1887, ending the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A resident commissioner, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melmoth-osborn">Sir Melmoth Osborn</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eshowe">Eshowe</a> through magistrates and appointed chiefs, and a hut tax was imposed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinuzulu-kacetshwayo">Dinuzulu</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetshwayo">Cetshwayo</a>, led resistance in 1888; he was tried for treason and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">St Helena</a>. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> men were drawn into migrant labour.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zululand</a> was annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal Colony</a> in December 1897. A land commission then opened much of it to white settlement, while the remaining reserves later formed the core of the KwaZulu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1887 CE – 1897 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:97.25%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1887 CE – 1897 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Eshowe</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Melmoth Osborn</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Zulu traditional religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiZulu, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>South Africa</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Colony of Zululand</dd></dl></aside></div>
